# MODE CERTIFICATE: maximum_relative_halfwidth 1e-6. At the earlier card's 1e-7 the first scan of the engine cut solve, on the start cut, was refused in window 1 at all four window counts, on the mode at 213.809 Hz, f1 on that cut: relative half-widths 5.05e-7, 2.51e-7, 9.02e-7 and 1.94e-7 at 10, 11, 12 and 13 windows (FS-MODAL-HALFWIDTH-EXCEEDED), the worst 9.02e-7. A relative half-width is the eigenvalue's, so at f1 the worst is 9.6e-5 Hz, 0.0008 c, and the 1e-6 row bounds it at 1.1e-4 Hz, 0.0009 c: a certificate tolerance two to three orders of magnitude below audibility. It sets no sound. 1e-6 is the next decade, as 1e-8 to 1e-7 was on the marimba and xylophone cards.
maximum_relative_halfwidth	1e-6
# RECEIVER: the broadband observer (e6313e19d): one delay and an order-16 rational fit of the boundary-element transfer from each bar mode to the receiver, checked on held-out frequencies against a 5 % budget. It hears the bar during the mallet's contact and with its travel time; the narrow-band law it replaces passed the contact force as a pulse.
observer	broadband
observer_fit_order	16
observer_held_out_budget	0.05
observer_rigid_rows	on
